WEBVTT

00:04:57.276 --> 00:05:00.556
with beauty and wonder and transcendence,

00:05:00.596 --> 00:05:03.236
the so-called sublime emotions.

00:05:03.236 --> 00:05:06.036
And you know, just think
of how many musical genres

00:05:06.076 --> 00:05:07.596
tap into sorrow, right.

00:05:07.636 --> 00:05:10.836
There’s Spanish flamenco
and Portuguese fado

00:05:10.876 --> 00:05:12.196
and the Irish lament

00:05:12.196 --> 00:05:15.396
and American country music and the blues.

00:05:15.396 --> 00:05:16.996
And then even lullabies,

00:05:17.036 --> 00:05:21.636
which all over the world we often use
our most heartbreaking melodies

00:05:21.676 --> 00:05:23.716
to sing our newborns to sleep.

00:05:23.756 --> 00:05:25.796
Why on Earth do we do that?

00:05:25.836 --> 00:05:27.436
(Laughter)

00:05:27.436 --> 00:05:29.196
And then it's not just music, right?

00:05:29.196 --> 00:05:31.796
We like rainy days and tragic drama